<task id="045" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Integrate auth-v4 from master so CI can run at all: migrate CallerRecordAccessProbe off its client secret, repair 5 Moq ctor sites, merge master</title>
    <phase>0b Review remediation</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies a live authorization seam (the OBO credential for the delegation gate on six external-access mutations plus Office save), and merges a large body of master into the branch. Highest blast radius of any task in this project.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-path credential change on an auth seam, plus a cross-project merge whose failure mode is silent (a broken OBO exchange denies every mutation).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <effort-reason>Brownfield root-cause work: the fix must be a faithful port of a reference impl that lives on the other side of a merge, and correctness cannot be observed offline (OBO needs a live tenant).</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Merges master and edits Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** plus four shared test fixtures. Nothing else may run concurrently.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>021</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Filed 2026-08-25. Found while pushing task 021: PR #812 is mergeable=CONFLICTING, and a conflicted PR dispatches NO workflows, so CI had been dark for two pushes. Resolving the conflict pulls master in, and a trial merge (aborted) produced 22 failures. Full diagnosis: notes/ci-dark-and-authv4-integration-2026-08-25.md.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>PR #812 cannot be CI-verified or merged to master until this lands. Merge origin/master, migrate CallerRecordAccessProbe off its self-built client-secret credential onto master's IConfidentialClientProvider, and repair the five Moq construction sites that master's widened DataverseWebApiClient constructor broke. Then confirm a check suite actually EXISTS before claiming anything is green.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in MSAL confidential clients, the on-behalf-of flow, and Dataverse OBO. Familiar with ADR-028 Amendment A4 (secret-free BFF identity).</role>

  <goal>PR #812 is mergeable, `CI / Router` renders an actual verdict on the branch, all seven test projects pass, and no secret-bearing confidential credential remains in this project's code. The delegation gate still denies when OBO is unavailable — the fail-closed direction is preserved, not traded away for a green build.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>READ notes/ci-dark-and-authv4-integration-2026-08-25.md FIRST. It contains the full diagnosis and the evidence.

WHY THIS IS URGENT AND NOT OPTIONAL. `ci-router.yml` triggers on `pull_request: branches: [master]`. When a PR is CONFLICTING, GitHub cannot compute `refs/pull/{n}/merge` and therefore dispatches NO workflows for it. This does not present as a red gate — it presents as NO gate, which is indistinguishable from "not started yet". Two commits (2035b1d16, 99408eee5) were pushed with zero adjudication before anyone noticed. Every local test result on this branch is currently unbacked by CI.

THE ORDERING IS FORCED. `IConfidentialClientProvider` exists only on master, so the merge MUST come first — the probe cannot be migrated before it. Sequence: merge, then fix, then verify.

CAUSE A -- the security-path change.
`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs` (created by task 008) builds its own MSAL confidential client at lines 133-138: `ConfidentialClientApplicationBuilder.Create(clientId).WithAuthority(...).WithClientSecret(clientSecret).Build()`, cached process-wide by (authority, clientId). Master's auth-v4 forcing functions both fail on it:
  - FR-F1 `CredentialGuardTests` -- "no secret-bearing confidential credential under src/server/** outside the allowlist"
  - FR-F2 `CredentialCensusTests` -- "UNLISTED confidential-client site in CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs"

This is item D1 with its premise expired. D1 was accepted 2026-08-23 as an ADR-028 A4 path-A exception "to be handled in the broader MI migration". auth-v4 IS that migration; it completed 2026-08-24 and CLOSED exception E-3 -- and it could not have handled this site, because the site lives on an unmerged branch and was invisible to it.

DO NOT ALLOWLIST IT. The census guard says so in its own failure message: "A failure here is NOT a prompt to update the number. The origin assessment for this project counted five confidential-client sites when there were eight, and the two it missed were found by a later audit rather than by anything automatic."

THE FIX IS A PORT, NOT A DESIGN. `DataverseUserClient` on master does exactly this job -- OBO through `IConfidentialClientProvider` -- and `CallerRecordAccessProbe`'s own comment already says it copied that class's caching shape. So: read master's `Services/Ai/Handlers/Dataverse/DataverseUserClient.cs` and port it faithfully. The contract is narrow:

    Task&lt;IConfidentialClientApplication&gt; GetClientAsync(string tenantId, string clientId, CancellationToken ct)

Note the consequence for the probe's constructor: it currently decides at CONSTRUCTION time whether OBO is possible (by checking for a secret) and sets `_cca = null` otherwise. With a provider the credential is resolved lazily and asynchronously, so that decision moves to call time. Preserve the behaviour, not the shape: when no credential can be obtained, the probe MUST still return `AccessRights.None` and log `DELEGATION-RPA-UNAVAILABLE`. There is deliberately NO app-only fallback -- an app-only probe would answer for the application rather than the caller, which is finding A-2's shape.

CAUSE B -- mechanical, ~20 failures, one root cause.
Master widened the constructor:

    public DataverseWebApiClient(IConfiguration configuration, ILogger&lt;DataverseWebApiClient&gt; logger,
        TokenCredential? credential = null, IConfidentialClientProvider? confidentialClients = null)

Moq requires an EXACT constructor match for a class proxy; optional parameters do not help. Every `new Mock&lt;DataverseWebApiClient&gt;(config, logger)` now throws `Can not instantiate proxy of class`. Five fixtures:
  tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/DelegationRuleTestFixture.cs
  tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/GrantLifecycleCharacterizationTests.cs
  tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ProjectClosureCascadeTests.cs
  tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/SpeRevokeMatcherTests.cs
  tests/integration/data-mutation/ExternalAccess/ProvisionProjectTestFixture.cs

THE MERGE CONFLICT is one hunk in `projects/INDEX.md`: master inserted the `spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI` row at the position this branch holds its own row. BOTH rows belong. Everything else auto-merges, including DataverseAccessDataSource.cs and ExternalAccessContractTests.cs.

FOLD IN while you are here (small, requested, and already stale):
The auth-v4 team left a comment on PR #812 (2026-08-24) asking for two corrections in `docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-ACCESS-LAYER-ROUTING.md` -- it still says the client-secret path is "retained as a local-dev fallback", which stopped being true on 2026-08-24 when the secret was deleted from app settings AND Key Vault. They supplied replacement wording in the comment. Also note `tests/e2e/.../secure-project-creation.spec.ts` defaults BFF_API_BASE to `spe-api-dev-67e2xz.azurewebsites.net`; the dev BFF is `spaarke-bff-dev`.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/Dataverse/DataverseUserClient.cs</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IConfidentialClientProvider.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/DelegationRuleTestFixture.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/GrantLifecycleCharacterizationTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ProjectClosureCascadeTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/SpeRevokeMatcherTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/data-mutation/ExternalAccess/ProvisionProjectTestFixture.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/INDEX.md</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-ACCESS-LAYER-ROUTING.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A4">NO new or retained secret-bearing confidential credential. Exception E-3 is CLOSED. Do not add a census or allowlist entry to make the guard pass -- the guard's own message argues against exactly that, and the census was wrong by three sites the last time someone updated a number instead of asking a question.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail-closed behaviour is NOT negotiable for a green build. If OBO cannot be performed, the probe returns AccessRights.None and the delegation gate DENIES. Do not introduce an app-only fallback: it would answer for the application rather than the caller, which is finding A-2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">PERTURBATION IS MANDATORY. At minimum: make the provider throw and confirm the gate denies rather than allows; return a client that yields no token and confirm the same. A zero-failure perturbation has THREE possible causes in this codebase -- wrong test level, unreachable code, or A FAKE THAT IGNORES PART OF THE CONTRACT (task 021's finding). Distinguish before touching a test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Run ALL SEVEN test projects. `dotnet test` at the root covers four; ArchTests, Spaarke.Core.Tests and RecordSyncJob.IsolatedTests need explicit invocation. On this task ArchTests is the one that matters most -- it holds FR-F1/FR-F2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">DO NOT claim CI is green without reading the gate. After pushing, verify a `github-actions` CHECK SUITE EXISTS for the SHA (`gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits/{sha}/check-suites`), then that `CI / Router` reached a conclusion. Absence of runs is a state to check for explicitly -- it looks exactly like success from a distance, and that is how two pushes went unadjudicated.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not push again while a run is in flight -- the Router takes ~25 min and uses cancel-in-progress, so a second push kills the first verdict.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF-touching: state the Placement Justification (this is a net credential-site DELETION, adding no component), report publish size vs the 43.70 MB baseline (ceiling 60), and confirm `--vulnerable --include-transitive` clean. Run /conflict-check first.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/ci-dark-and-authv4-integration-2026-08-25.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-008-delegation-rule.md</file>
