      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Read the diagnosis note. Run /conflict-check. Confirm PR #812 is still CONFLICTING and that no check suite exists for HEAD -- if a suite now exists, the situation has changed and this task needs re-scoping before you touch anything.</step>
    <step order="1">Merge origin/master. Resolve the single `projects/INDEX.md` conflict by KEEPING BOTH rows, and refresh this project's row while there. Do NOT commit yet.</step>
    <step order="2">Read master's `DataverseUserClient` in full -- it is the reference impl for OBO via IConfidentialClientProvider. Note how it handles credential exhaustion.</step>
    <step order="3">Port `CallerRecordAccessProbe` onto `IConfidentialClientProvider`. Delete the `WithClientSecret` builder and the process-wide CcaCache if the provider already caches. Move the "can we do OBO at all?" decision from construction time to call time WITHOUT changing the observable outcome: no credential still means AccessRights.None plus the DELEGATION-RPA-UNAVAILABLE marker.</step>
    <step order="4">Repair the five Moq construction sites for the widened DataverseWebApiClient constructor.</step>
    <step order="5">Build with --warnaserror. Run ALL SEVEN test projects. FR-F1 and FR-F2 in ArchTests must both pass, and no test may have been weakened to achieve it.</step>
    <step order="6">Perturb per the constraint: provider throws; provider returns a client that cannot mint a token. Both must DENY, and each must fail at least one test. Record counts.</step>
    <step order="7">Apply the two DATAVERSE-ACCESS-LAYER-ROUTING.md corrections the auth-v4 comment requested, using their supplied wording.</step>
    <step order="8">Report publish size and CVE status. Commit the merge and the fixes.</step>
    <step order="9">Push, then WAIT. Verify (a) a github-actions check suite exists for the SHA, (b) PR #812 is no longer CONFLICTING, (c) `CI / Router` reaches a conclusion. Report the ACTUAL verdict -- and if the Router is red for a reason that looks unrelated to this diff, chase it rather than routing around it.</step>
    <step order="10">Update notes, TASK-INDEX and current-task.md. If the Router is green, say plainly that this is the FIRST CI-verified state of the branch since ffc2cb1de.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the ported probe cannot obtain a credential in ANY configuration reachable offline, STOP before pushing and say so. OBO correctness is not observable without a live tenant; do not report "works" on the strength of a unit test that never performs an exchange. Task 034 owns live verification.</trigger>
    <trigger>If master's merge turns out to have changed the delegation gate's behaviour (not just its credential), STOP -- that is a behavioural change to an authorization path and needs an owner decision, not a merge resolution.</trigger>
    <trigger>If FR-F1/FR-F2 still fail after the port, do NOT add an allowlist/census entry to go green. Report what the guard is objecting to and why.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>CallerRecordAccessProbe already exists (task 008) and already performs OBO; master already provides IConfidentialClientProvider and a working consumer of it.</existing>
    <extension>Net deletion: one credential construction site removed, replaced by an injected dependency that already exists. No new service, interface, or package.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>PR #812 cannot be CI-verified or merged AT ALL -- a conflicted PR dispatches no workflows, so every local result on this branch is unbacked and the work cannot reach master or be deployed. Separately, the branch would carry the ninth secret-bearing confidential client into a codebase that deleted the secret from Key Vault on 2026-08-24, so the credential would not resolve in any deployed environment.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/*.cs (5 ctor sites)</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/ci-dark-and-authv4-integration-2026-08-25.md</output>
    <output type="doc">docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-ACCESS-LAYER-ROUTING.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>PR #812 reports mergeable != CONFLICTING.</criterion>
    <criterion>A github-actions check suite EXISTS for the pushed SHA, and `CI / Router` reaches a conclusion that is reported verbatim.</criterion>
    <criterion>ArchTests FR-F1 and FR-F2 both pass with NO new allowlist or census entry.</criterion>
    <criterion>No `.WithClientSecret` or `ClientSecretCredential` remains anywhere in this project's changed code.</criterion>
    <criterion>All seven test projects pass; the five Moq ctor sites are repaired.</criterion>
    <criterion>With no obtainable credential the delegation gate DENIES -- proven by a test, not asserted.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every perturbation fails at least one test; counts recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion>Publish size reported and &lt;=60 MB compressed incl. PDBs; --vulnerable clean.</criterion>
    <criterion>The two DATAVERSE-ACCESS-LAYER-ROUTING.md corrections are applied.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>This task exists because a conflicted PR produces NO gate rather than a red one — a failure mode worth remembering independently of this project. It must run BEFORE any further Phase 0/0b work, because nothing on this branch can be CI-verified until it lands.</notes>
</task>
